59,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option C removes the concept of ownership. It eliminates the ""my spot"" resentment entirely.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Option B feels the most fair on paper. Everyone gets a chance, no one is favored.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option C is the only one that solves the morning shoving. No one is guarding a spot.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A is the only one that generates money. But who collects it?,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A requires a collector. Option B requires a clerk. Option C requires nothing.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, exactly. Option C is self-enforcing. If you don't use it, someone else does.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"But @Ryuji, what about the rain? If everyone uses the same racks, the dry spots are still contested.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"The racks are double-tier. The rain is a fact, but the shoving is a choice.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,Option A is a trap. We have no treasurer. We will just have debt.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,Option B is a trap. The clerk will quit after the first dispute.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,Option C creates a shared space. It forces cooperation rather than competition.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I worry that the people who ride daily will feel their rights are being ignored.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,The daily riders are the ones causing the shoving. Option C stops that.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,Option C costs zero. It is the only rational choice for a broke building.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,Option C requires zero maintenance. It is the only sustainable choice.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote for C. It is the only option that preserves social harmony.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I vote for B. It is the only option that feels truly fair to everyone.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for C. It is the only option that respects the physical reality.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I vote for C. It is the only option that respects the financial reality.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I vote for C. It is the only option that respects the administrative reality.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
